      "writtenOn": "2022-02-16T21:54:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Callbacks look good, but there are some issues with how exceptions are handled. \n\nThe general rule is that\n1. App API calls should never crash system service. Hence, we should not throw RemoteException when failed to call App callback from HapClientService\n2. When App calls system service, if there is a RemoteException, it should be rethrowFromSystemServer() instead of silently handle it in the API class. This help App become aware that the system service is having trouble. \n3. In Binder.Stub() context, some exceptions will be passed back to the caller, they include: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Parcel#writeException(java.lang.Exception)\n\nBadParcelableException\nIllegalArgumentException\nIllegalStateException\nNullPointerException\nSecurityException\nUnsupportedOperationException\nNetworkOnMainThreadException\n\nPlease only throw these exceptions in incoming binder context",
      "revId": "db391d2076b38c39f317c0fb44fd0ac98ab09e8f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
